## Summary

Built a complete local web app at `/Users/lily/dev/pi-bench/experiments/evaluator-no-rewrite/claude-workspace/` that satisfies every PRD requirement:

**Architecture**
- `lib/anserini.js` — thin wrapper around `java -cp $ANSERINI_JAR …` for `PrebuiltIndexRegistry`, `TopicsRegistry`, `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes`, `SearchCollection`, `TrecEval`. Never mocks.
- `lib/catalog.js` — pulls 109 inverted indexes from the registry, parses the 17 shipped reproduction-config YAMLs, tokenizes each `command:` template, substitutes `$topics`, and derives every (index → topics → eval_key → metric_definitions) pairing dynamically. CACM lights up as evaluable purely from the `cacm` reproduction config — no hardcoded pairings.
- `server.js` — Express app exposing `/api/health`, `/api/catalog`, `/api/evaluate`, `/api/artifacts/:name`, with in-memory catalog cache and structured error reporting.
- `public/` — vanilla HTML/CSS/JS UI: filterable catalog (109 indexes, 99 evaluable, 10 catalog-only badged), per-index detail, pairing selector, metric selector that promotes `nDCG@10` / `Recall@1000`, Run Evaluation button, score display, evaluator output, run-file preview, and the actual commands invoked.
- `tests/e2e.spec.js` + `playwright.config.js` — Playwright e2e that auto-starts the server, asserts >10 indexes, CACM auto-selected, ≥1 catalog-only entry, nDCG@10 selectable, real numeric score in [0,1], all metadata fields present, and crucially **anti-mock checks** on the displayed `io.anserini.*` commands, `anserini-*-fatjar.jar` reference, `trec_eval`-shaped `\tall\t<score>` output, and TREC-format run lines on disk.

**Verified end-to-end**
- Health: Java 21.0.11 + `anserini-2.1.1-fatjar.jar` ✓
- Catalog: 109 inverted indexes, 99 evaluable, 17 reproduce configs ✓
- CACM nDCG@10 = **0.4543** (matches expected) in ~1.4s retrieval + 0.2s eval ✓
- Playwright passes from a clean state in ~6 s ✓

**Run it**
```bash
npm install
npm start              # http://localhost:4317
npm run test:e2e       # Playwright e2e
```